                <pb facs="0251" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9402: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-10T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>341. Your No. 862, September 8, 4 p.m. Merely send the Foreign Office a
                    third-person acknowledgment stating that contents of the note relating to
                    withdrawing of troops have been communicated to your Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
